*.pyc
*.pyo
__pycache__/

# Fetched image BYTES, not the index. 1.37 GB of COCO train2017 JPEGs in zstd parquet
# shards, regenerable from coco_fetch_train2017/fetch_list.parquet by download_coco_images.py
# and verifiable against the sha256 stored beside each payload.
#
# The index IS tracked, deliberately: the same rule the pose datasets got, where a Google
# Drive folder cannot be a manifest <project> and what satisfies the Sides rule is an index
# in git rather than the bytes.
coco_images_train2017/

# The pixi environments. Covered today only by `.pixi/.gitignore`, which PIXI WRITES and
# which reads `*` then `!config.toml` -- so the tool's own file is the only thing keeping
# gigabytes of solved environment out, and it deliberately un-ignores one path inside.
# Pinned here so the rule survives the directory being recreated, and so it is visible in
# a diff rather than in a generated file nobody reviews.
.pixi/
